+## Global planner microbenchmark
+
+The planner benchmark is independent from the odometry-based navigation
+evaluation below. It starts only a static map server, planner server, planner
+lifecycle manager, and static transforms, then calls
+`ComputePathToPose` with an explicit start pose.
+
+Validate the versioned Hospital query set without starting ROS nodes:
+
+```bash
+ros2 run arena_evaluation planner_benchmark \
+  --protocol $(ros2 pkg prefix arena_evaluation)/share/arena_evaluation/config/planner_benchmark_protocol.yaml \
+  --queries $(ros2 pkg prefix arena_evaluation)/share/arena_evaluation/config/planner_benchmark_queries_hospital.yaml \
+  --output-dir /home/robot/pudu_robot_ws/experiments/planner_benchmark/hospital/validation \
+  --validate-only
+```
+
+Run one planner/variant, or use `all` for both dimensions. `--query-id` may be
+repeated for a smoke subset; omitting it runs the complete query file.
+
+```bash
+ros2 run arena_evaluation planner_benchmark \
+  --protocol $(ros2 pkg prefix arena_evaluation)/share/arena_evaluation/config/planner_benchmark_protocol.yaml \
+  --queries $(ros2 pkg prefix arena_evaluation)/share/arena_evaluation/config/planner_benchmark_queries_hospital.yaml \
+  --output-dir /home/robot/pudu_robot_ws/experiments/planner_benchmark/hospital/RUN_ID \
+  --planner all --config-variant all
+
+ros2 run arena_evaluation planner_benchmark_report \
+  --dir /home/robot/pudu_robot_ws/experiments/planner_benchmark/hospital/RUN_ID
+```
+
+Product preserves the Arena planner semantics, including DUBIN for Smac
+Hybrid. Normalized uses a common footprint, static/inflation costmap,
+`allow_unknown=false`, tolerance 0.25 m, and REEDS_SHEPP for Smac Hybrid.
+Successful paths are stored separately from `odom.csv`; `planner_runs.csv`
+uses explicit `run_id`, `query_id`, `planner_id`, and `config_variant` keys.
+
 The Arena Evaluation package provides tools to record, evaluate, and plot navigational metrics to evaluate ROS navigation planners. It is best suited for usage with our [arena-rosnav repository](https://github.com/Arena-Rosnav/arena-rosnav) but can also be integrated into any other ROS-based project.
 
